  "decisions": [
   "D9-01 EBM on the curated-20 first-visit feature set",
   "D9-02 measured waist replaced by a clinician-assessed 3-level adiposity band (published WHtR boundaries 0.50/0.60); required field, no blank level"
  ],
  "limitations": [
   "F9-05 the calibration layer is isotonic recalibration with Venn-Abers-style endpoints, an APPROXIMATION of inductive Venn-Abers. It carries no distribution-free guarantee.",
   "F9-06 conformal coverage is measured under a temporal split, which violates exchangeability by design. Do not claim a 90% per-class coverage guarantee.",
   "F9-08 HbA1c is not a neutral measure of glycaemia: it responds to MCH (-0.0448, p~4e-235) and RDW independently of glucose. No CBC feature is in this model, so that bias is unmodelled noise rather than a misleading explanation -- but it is not removed.",
   "F9-09 excluding race as an input does NOT make the model race-blind; the 20 shipped features recover NH Black / NH Asian membership at the AUCs reported in metrics.race_recoverability.",
   "F9-10 sensitivity and AUC vary strongly by age band; see metrics.fairness.",
   "F9-11 calibration differs by ethnic group behind an acceptable pooled number; see metrics.fairness.",
   "F9-12 NHANES cohort prevalence is 32.9%. This is a US screening cohort. No matched Jordanian figure for HbA1c >= 5.7 among the undiagnosed and untreated has been sourced. Absolute probabilities require local recalibration before they are displayed.",
   "F9-25 in training data, an absent adiposity measurement is itself a risk signal (prevalence 0.389 vs 0.279 in the 'increased' band). The deployed field is REQUIRED for this reason."
